# Line-ending policy (added 2026-08-30).
#
# Why this file exists: the repo is edited from a Windows laptop, a Linux
# container, and a WSL/remote shell. Without a policy, whichever machine last
# saved a file rewrites every line in it, and `git diff` fills with noise that
# hides the one line that actually changed. That is the same failure mode
# docs/environment.md exists to fight — a second place state can silently
# diverge — so it gets the same treatment: pin it once, in the repo.
#
# Policy: LF in the repository and in the working tree, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exception: PowerShell scripts are run by Windows-native tooling; keep CRLF
# in the working tree. They are still stored as LF in the repository.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.parquet binary
